* dual_mosfet.lib
* Subcircuit models for dual-MOSFET packages (SOT-23-6)
*
* NMOS_WST3392 — dual N-ch MOSFET (SOT-23-6L)
*   Package pins: 1=G1, 2=S1, 3=G2, 4=D2, 5=S2, 6=D1
*   KiCad Sim.Pins = "1 2 6 3 5 4"  (order: g1 s1 d1 g2 s2 d2)
*
* PMOS_WST2011 — dual P-ch MOSFET (SOT-23-6L)
*   Same package pinout as NMOS_WST3392
*   KiCad Sim.Pins = "1 2 6 3 5 4"

* Generic N-ch MOSFET (Level 1, approximates small-signal NMOS)
.model GENERIC_NMOS NMOS (Level=1 Kp=100m Vto=1.5 Lambda=0.02 Gamma=0 Phi=0.6
+  Cgso=20p Cgdo=5p Cbd=10p Cbs=10p)

* Generic P-ch MOSFET (Level 1, approximates small-signal PMOS)
.model GENERIC_PMOS PMOS (Level=1 Kp=40m Vto=-1.5 Lambda=0.02 Gamma=0 Phi=0.6
+  Cgso=20p Cgdo=5p Cbd=10p Cbs=10p)

* NMOS_WST3392: dual N-channel, independent transistors
* Port order: g1 s1 d1 g2 s2 d2
.subckt NMOS_WST3392 g1 s1 d1 g2 s2 d2
M1 d1 g1 s1 s1 GENERIC_NMOS
M2 d2 g2 s2 s2 GENERIC_NMOS
.ends NMOS_WST3392

* PMOS_WST2011: dual P-channel, independent transistors
* Port order: g1 s1 d1 g2 s2 d2
.subckt PMOS_WST2011 g1 s1 d1 g2 s2 d2
M1 d1 g1 s1 s1 GENERIC_PMOS
M2 d2 g2 s2 s2 GENERIC_PMOS
.ends PMOS_WST2011
